# mayhem/build.sh deliberately writes EVERY build artifact to $SRC/target/mayhem (the repo-root
# target/ tree, already ignored by oxc's own .gitignore) so that nothing compiled ever lands under
# mayhem/. That placement is load-bearing, not cosmetic: the conformance gate content-greps this
# directory RECURSIVELY for the forbidden __asan/__lsan option-override symbol names, and an
# ASan-linked Rust binary carries those strings in its own symbol table — a cargo target/ dir left
# anywhere under mayhem/ hard-FAILs a perfectly clean integration.
#
# The entries below are belt-and-braces for anyone who runs cargo by hand inside mayhem/fuzz or
# mayhem/kat without going through build.sh.
build-out/
fuzz/target/
kat/target/
